# RUN: %stinkytofu-opt --arch gfx1250 %s --LiftAsmRegistersToSSAPass=classes=v --RegisterAllocationPass=allocator=greedy-compact,classes=v,report,apply,matrix=auto --remarks --print-output 2>&1
#
# matrix=auto, end to end, on the kernel of
# allocation_rule_producer_shape_matrix_test.stir.
#
# Auto tries placing the matrix operands by shape first, and that colours this
# kernel, so the pin is never tried. The report names the attempt that won and
# the rules it set, and the registers are the ones naming the shape rule gives:
# the chain on v[8:15] and both rounds of A on v[0:7], not the producer's
# v[100:107] and v[300:307].
#
# CHECK: matrix[auto shape]
# CHECK-SAME: rule[ProducerPinMatrix=off] rule[ProducerShapeMatrix=active] rule[ProducerPinAccumulator=off]
# CHECK-NOT: placing them by shape was refused
# CHECK-LABEL: st.func @allocation_matrix_policy
# CHECK: v[0:3] = "st.ds_load_b128"
# CHECK-NEXT: v[4:7] = "st.ds_load_b128"
# CHECK-NEXT: v[8:15] = "st.v_wmma_f32_16x16x32_bf16"(v[0:7], v[16:23], v[8:15])
# CHECK-NEXT: v[0:3] = "st.ds_load_b128"
# CHECK-NEXT: v[4:7] = "st.ds_load_b128"
# CHECK-NEXT: v[8:15] = "st.v_wmma_f32_16x16x32_bf16"(v[0:7], v[16:23], v[8:15])
# CHECK-NEXT: "st.v_add_f32"(v8, v9)

st.func @allocation_matrix_policy() {
^entry:
  v[300:303] = "st.ds_load_b128"(v50) { mod.ds = { na = 1, offset = 0, gds = false } }
  v[304:307] = "st.ds_load_b128"(v50) { mod.ds = { na = 1, offset = 16, gds = false } }
  v[100:107] = "st.v_wmma_f32_16x16x32_bf16"(v[300:307], v[320:327], v[100:107])
  v[300:303] = "st.ds_load_b128"(v51) { mod.ds = { na = 1, offset = 0, gds = false } }
  v[304:307] = "st.ds_load_b128"(v51) { mod.ds = { na = 1, offset = 16, gds = false } }
  v[100:107] = "st.v_wmma_f32_16x16x32_bf16"(v[300:307], v[320:327], v[100:107])
  v40 = "st.v_add_f32"(v100, v101)
  "st.s_endpgm"()
}
